From: ouroboros420 <ouroboros420@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a6xx: drop the boot bandwidth vote once the GMU votes

a6xx_gmu_resume() places a host gfx-mem vote at the OPP the GPU resumes
at so the GMU can boot ("bus quota ... for boot"). With GMU bandwidth
voting, a6xx_gmu_set_freq() then leaves the host vote alone because the
GMU votes for all resources, so the boot vote stays until runtime
suspend, which does not happen while frames keep coming. RPMh takes the
max of the host and GMU votes, so DDR cannot drop below the resume
level for a whole gaming session.

Drop the host vote once the GMU has acked its own vote. The GMU votes
from the same OPP bandwidth table, so the active level is unchanged; the
only difference is that DDR now follows the GMU instead of a stale floor.
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
index db36249..51a7531 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -225,10 +225,13 @@ void a6xx_gmu_set_freq(struct msm_gpu *gpu, struct dev_pm_opp *opp,
 		return;
 
 	if (!gmu->legacy) {
-		a6xx_hfi_set_freq(gmu, perf_index, bw_index);
+		ret = a6xx_hfi_set_freq(gmu, perf_index, bw_index);
 		/* With Bandwidth voting, we now vote for all resources, so skip OPP set */
 		if (!bw_index)
 			dev_pm_opp_set_opp(&gpu->pdev->dev, opp);
+		/* ...and drop the vote a6xx_gmu_set_initial_bw() placed for GMU boot */
+		else if (!ret)
+			dev_pm_opp_set_opp(&gpu->pdev->dev, NULL);
 		return;
 	}
 
